x86_64-linux  cxx1 moves the temporary `return Q(...)` builds into the caller's object through the implicit move constructor, where clang elides it - [class.copy]/31 permits both - so cxx1 emits Q<3>'s and V<3>'s move constructors and clang does not. It also emits the C1 forms clang does not, the difference move-constructor.nonames records.
x86_64-windows  cxx1 moves the temporary `return Q(...)` builds into the caller's object through the implicit move constructor, where clang elides it - [class.copy]/31 permits both - so cxx1 emits Q<3>'s and V<3>'s move constructors and clang does not.
arm64-darwin  cxx1 moves the temporary `return Q(...)` builds into the caller's object through the implicit move constructor, where clang elides it - [class.copy]/31 permits both - so cxx1 emits Q<3>'s and V<3>'s move constructors and clang does not.
